+      "_whines": "single ricochets cut at their own onsets (measured: each rises 10 dB or more within 10 ms) out of rakurka's Incoming Ricochets (approved as bullets_incoming_01/02): twelve whines from one approved recording, so the same one is rarely heard twice. From 21 Nov (round eight, Good at 21:41Z): Benboncan's three ricochet whines (CC BY 4.0), whole, each falling in pitch (about 700 to 500 Hz, and 1.1 kHz). Each opened with a 2 ms tick 17 to 20 dB over its whine (the strike: here the earth's or the steel's own take is the strike), so each starts just after it, and its first 0.3 s sits at the median of the twelve (-26.6 dB; as recorded they were 8 to 14 dB under). ricochet_02 and 03 (the strike with a short whine) were Cut: `ricochet` keeps ricochet_01",
